WEBVTT

00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:10.917
This video shows how to create an exam type on your phone. Exam types are the categories of exams your school runs, like Unit Test, Mid-Term and Final.

00:00:12.597 --> 00:00:22.845
Tap the menu button at the top left, open Academics, and then choose Exam Types. Each existing exam type is a card showing its name and its weight.

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:30.729
Tap Add Exam Type at the top of the page. A form opens asking for a name and a weight.

00:00:31.607 --> 00:00:41.159
Type the name, here Unit Test. Then set the weight to 30. The weight is how much this exam counts toward the final result.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:56.554
Below the weight is the Final exam option. Tick it only for exams that decide promotion. We leave it unticked, because a unit test does not decide promotion.

00:00:57.021 --> 00:01:05.061
Tap Create. A message confirms the new exam type, and its card appears in the list with a 30 percent weight.

00:01:08.189 --> 00:01:13.877
Your exam type is ready. You can now use it when you create exams.
